## From https://jasonstitt.com/gitignore-whitelisting-patterns

# 1. Ignore everything
*

# 2. But descend into directories
!*/

# 3. Allow specific files and file extensions
!.gitignore
!requirements.txt
!*.py
!*.md
!*.png
!*.yml
!*.yaml
!*.env.example
!devcontainer.json
!Dockerfile
!data/datasets/basic_pdfs/sample.pdf
!data/prompts/basic.txt

# 4. Block some directories and files
*.git
**/*env
**/.venv
**/TMP

# Keep personal deliverables and runtime evidence outside public commits.
/docs/artifacts/
/docs/interactions/
/.private/
/private-data/
/privacy-backups/
/data/private/
/data/results/
